  "caption": "Quinn's leg felt like a zappy cable from bum to calf, so the plan was to stay in bed until it left. By day 4, everything felt stiffer and crankier.\n\nSciatica often responds better to calm, controlled movement than to bed rest. Lots of rest can stiffen tissues and make the nerve more sensitive.\n\nWhat can help: gentle nerve \"sliders\" first (tensioners come later), finding the spinal movement direction that draws leg pain back toward the back, deep trunk work, and keeping everyday activity going at a pace you can tolerate.\n\nGet help straight away for numbness or weakness in both legs, bladder or bowel changes, numbness in the saddle area, or weakness that is quickly getting worse.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
